1
00:00:00,384 --> 00:00:03,968
At the sight of thee, how my heart doth sing...

2
00:00:04,672 --> 00:00:08,470
...Oh, to soar the wind on a silver wing

3
00:00:10,501 --> 00:00:12,096
Back when I made that promise

4
00:00:12,369 --> 00:00:14,656
I don't think it was for my nation's sake

5
00:00:16,064 --> 00:00:17,786
A free spirit like me?

6
00:00:18,112 --> 00:00:20,416
I just longed for her gaze

7
00:00:23,190 --> 00:00:25,099
But at some point along the way

8
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:27,584
The landscape reflected in her eyes

9
00:00:27,725 --> 00:00:30,080
Became another thing I held dear

10
00:00:36,611 --> 00:00:39,500
I feared this scenery might fade from her eyes

11
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:41,625
Leaving her only grief and sorrow

12
00:00:42,374 --> 00:00:45,354
I couldn't bear the thought, couldn't let go...

13
00:00:45,525 --> 00:00:48,225
Even though it led me to the state I'm in now

14
00:00:49,375 --> 00:00:53,471
But I've always known... nothing lasts forever...

15
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:58,591
As seasons churn, the swallows fair

16
00:00:59,025 --> 00:01:02,771
From radiance return to uttermost airs

17
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:08,342
The long road ahead lies ruined, lost

18
00:01:08,375 --> 00:01:11,635
The straight lane by error and treachery toss'd

19
00:01:11,763 --> 00:01:15,917
Depart, virtuous soul! Why let fondness seize your lingering thought?

20
00:01:15,917 --> 00:01:19,887
Why upset slumber with that which must come unwrought?

21
00:01:19,987 --> 00:01:21,887
Depart, O soul

22
00:01:21,887 --> 00:01:26,362
Depart, and sorrow not

23
00:01:28,575 --> 00:01:32,577
Where shall they return? The swallows nest together

24
00:01:32,897 --> 00:01:36,971
Whither shall they meet? The silver lamps glimmer

25
00:01:37,227 --> 00:01:42,067
I wake from dreams. The jade pin parted, the dark birds flown, the clouds they drift on by

26
00:01:42,067 --> 00:01:45,300
The rain-bell rings, yet who shall hear?

27
00:01:45,725 --> 00:01:49,669
Youth blushes, alas, and fair faces dear

28
00:01:49,669 --> 00:01:53,614
Still the green mountains' fastness turns my head

29
00:01:53,864 --> 00:01:55,427
But why?

30
00:01:55,550 --> 00:01:58,250
Have I failed you, or been failed instead?

31
00:01:58,250 --> 00:01:59,239
I never once imagined

32
00:01:59,239 --> 00:02:00,886
That, a thousand years on

33
00:02:00,886 --> 00:02:05,933
This humble tea stand would once again bring together such a group of young talents

34
00:02:07,616 --> 00:02:08,877
Just like us back then

35
00:02:09,525 --> 00:02:11,791
Raising blades to purge evil

36
00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:15,725
Protecting this beautiful land

37
00:02:16,176 --> 00:02:17,715
Just as she wished

38
00:02:20,814 --> 00:02:22,701
I was a fool to worry so much

39
00:02:23,405 --> 00:02:27,309
In Liyue... things have always been this way

40
00:02:35,357 --> 00:02:38,886
Moonlight beckons, swallows fly

41
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:41,693
Basking in the endless sky

42
00:02:43,450 --> 00:02:45,476
You need not be like us...

43
00:02:46,215 --> 00:02:49,261
May you walk your own path

